#: src/ui/macro_editor.c:44
msgid ""
"Action: the data sent on the port. Plain text, plus the escapes \\r "
"(carriage return), \\n (line feed), \\t (tab), \\a, \\b, \\f, \\v, \\\\ "
"(backslash) and \\xHH (one byte in hexadecimal, e.g. \\x0D).\n"
"\n"
"Arguments: each specifier gets a field in the macro panel; its value is "
"remembered in the macros file. %d %i (integer), %u %o %x %X (unsigned), %f "
"%e %g %a (decimal number), %c (character), %s (text), with optional flags, "
"width, precision and length (e.g. %02X, %.3f, %ld); %% sends a percent sign. "
"%#Name picks a value from the list \"Name\" of the Lists page; a macro whose "
"only argument is a list of exactly two values shows two buttons.\n"
"\n"
"Separators: the action %& draws a line in the panel, [Title] %& a line with "
"a title.\n"
"\n"
"Tab: the panel tab of the macro (empty: General). A macro without label or "
"action is not shown in the panel; its shortcut still works.\n"
"\n"
"Shortcut: select a macro, click \"Capture Shortcut\", then press the keys "
"(Ctrl, Alt or Super with a key, or a function key alone); Escape cancels. A "
"shortcut already used by the application or by another macro is refused.\n"
"\n"
"Polling: right-click a macro button in the panel for \"Polling Mode\" and "
"its period (1 to 86400000 ms); a click then starts or stops the repeated "
"sending. Right-click the tab bar to hide or show tabs; hiding a tab stops "
"its polling.\n"
"\n"
"Examples: \"Hello\\n\" sends Hello and a line feed; \"Hello\\x0A\" does the "
"same; \"SPEED %d\\r\" asks for a number."
msgstr ""

